  "category" : "Assessment and Accountability",
  "createdAt" : 1729873211,
  "description" : "This dataset contains results from the legacy MCAS assessment administered between 2007-2022, including achievement level, participation rate, average scaled score, and median student growth percentile. Data is available for the following years and subjects:\n<ul><li>Grades 3-8 ELA and math: 2007-2016</li><li>Grade 10 ELA and math: 2007-2018</li><li>Grades 5 and 8 STE: 2007-2018</li><li>High school science: 2007-2022</li></ul>The Massachusetts Comprehensive Assessment System (MCAS) is a statewide assessment administered to help parents, students, educators, and policymakers determine where districts, schools, and students are meeting expectations and where they need additional support. For more information about MCAS data, please visit the <a href=\"https://profiles.doe.mass.edu/help/data.aspx?section=assess\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Profiles Help - About the Data</a> page.\n\nCurrent (“Next Gen”) MCAS results can be found in the <a href=\"https://educationtocareer.data.mass.gov/Assessment-and-Accountability/MCAS-Achievement-Results/i9w6-niyt/about_data\">MCAS Achievement Results</a> dataset. PARCC results can be found on the Department of Elementary and Secondary Education's <a href=\"https://profiles.doe.mass.edu/statereport/parcc.aspx\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Profiles site</a>. Results from different assessment systems measure different standards and cannot be directly compared. Please see the DESE Researcher's Guide linked as featured content below for more information.\n\nStudent growth percentile (MEDIAN_SGP) was calculated as a median prior to 2018. Since 2018, it has been calculated as a mean. In 2021, following the COVID-19 pandemic, a baseline SGP method was used to compare growth from 2019 to 2021. For all other years, a cohort referenced model has been used. For more information on SGP calculations, please see the <a href=\"https://www.doe.mass.edu/mcas/growth\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Student Growth</a> page on DESE's website.\n\nThis dataset contains the same data that is also published on our DESE Profiles site:\n<a href=\"https://profiles.doe.mass.edu/statereport/legacymcas.aspx\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Legacy MCAS Achievement Results</a>",
